@@ -0,0 +1,5 @@
+---
+'@radix-ui/react-slot': patch
+---
+
+Fixed infinite re-render loop in React 19 caused by `Slot` creating a new ref callback on every render. The composed ref is now memoized via `useComposedRefs`, so ref callbacks (e.g. ones that trigger state updates, like those used by editors such as Slate/Plate) are no longer re-invoked on every render, which previously led to "Maximum update depth exceeded" errors.
